{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"8638e33e-a9b5-495d-bbb2-533aa9a7eec3","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The fix has been applied to [gen.py](file:///tmp/h-blbIy8/gen.py) and documentation of the changes has been written to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-blbIy8/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **[gen.py](file:///tmp/h-blbIy8/gen.py)**:\n   - Changed the lower-bound field name in `hr_target` from `\"value\"` to `\"start\"`, producing `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\n   - When exporting FIT files to Garmin, Intervals.icu uses `{start, end}` for an Instant-HR corridor (which preserves the raw bpm calculated from Intervals' LTHR), whereas `{value, end}` routes as a Lap-HR target that gets clamped to the watch's local zones.\n\n2. **[ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-blbIy8/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Details what was changed and why.\n   - Clarifies which parts of the colleague's note applied (the key rename from `value` to `start` and retaining `%lthr` units) versus which parts were ignored (text-grammar description rules and instructions for manual API sync / test event creation).\n","duration_seconds":40.813027,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":89373,"output_tokens":1873,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":97010,"total_tokens":91246}}}
